.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:5:- **Wave / agents:** W2-A (DOS-209 — `ServiceContext` + `ExecutionMode`) and W2-B (DOS-259 — `IntelligenceProvider` trait + PTY/Glean migration). Both blocked at L0 cycle 2.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:27:- **codex challenge (ESCALATE):** Plan v2 §7 says "W2-B opens/lands first." DOS-209 Linear ticket Dependencies block says: *"Landing order: this issue first; then IntelligenceProvider trait extraction (separate issue, in parallel); then everything else."* Plan author flipped the frozen contract per wave-plan hint, which is not authority to override the Linear ticket.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:35:- **codex consult (REVISE, fresh F2):** Plan v2 §3 freezes `select_provider(ctx: &ServiceContext, tier)`. DOS-259 ticket text says *"Transform abilities take `&dyn IntelligenceProvider` via `AbilityContext`."* ADR-0104 splits: `ServiceContext` carries mode + clients; provider injected via `AbilityContext`. Cycle-1 F3 fix landed the routing on the wrong context.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:37:**Independent verifiability:** Read DOS-259 ticket §"Architectural surfaces touched" — explicit statement "Transform abilities take `&dyn IntelligenceProvider` via `AbilityContext`." Plan v2 contradicts this surface.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:48:- **Provider seam:** Putting `select_provider(ctx: &ServiceContext, ...)` on the wrong context means W3-B (Provenance), W4-B (eval harness), and post-spine DOS-213 (prompt fingerprinting) consumers will need to invent a bridge or the plan will need a v3 architectural pass after v2 is "frozen."
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:54:- **W3 dependency:** W3-A (registry), W3-B (claims), W3-C (DOS-7) all consume W2-A's `ServiceContext` and W2-B's `IntelligenceProvider`. Every day W2 doesn't freeze pushes W3 right.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:60:- **Provider seam:** moderate one-way door. If `select_provider` ships on `ServiceContext`, downstream consumers can route around it via additional plumbing, but the architecturally-correct seam (`AbilityContext`) becomes the path of last resort, not first. ADR-0104 already specified the right answer; this is a "re-read the ADR and align" fix, not a research project.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:74:   - Move `select_provider` signature to take `&AbilityContext` (or whatever the equivalent W3-A registry-derived context is). Acknowledge that for early callers (intel_queue, services/intelligence.rs) that don't yet have an `AbilityContext`, the routing happens via an `AppState`-owned provider Arc per ADR-0091, and the factory only runs in ability-execution contexts.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:75:   - State explicitly that `ServiceContext.execution_mode` is the only thing the factory reads from `ServiceContext`; everything else is `AbilityContext`-owned.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:80:- **1A: Amend DOS-209 ticket.** Update the Linear Dependencies block: "Landing order amended 2026-04-28 per wave-plan hint and architectural review: W2-B (DOS-259, IntelligenceProvider trait extraction) opens its PR first to reduce the mutation surface; W2-A rebases on top." This is the cleanest fix; aligns ticket with wave plan + plan v2.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:88:Discard plan v2, rebuild plan v1 from scratch with explicit pre-L0 architectural alignment from a domain expert pass on ADR-0104 ServiceContext / AbilityContext split. Adds 2–3 days. Justified only if Option A's tightly-scoped cycle 3 fails or if the architectural questions are deeper than the cycle-2 reviewers caught.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:92:Ship plan v2 as-frozen. File three follow-up issues for v1.4.1: (1) Re-audit DOS-209 mutation catalogue post-W2 ship; (2) Re-route DOS-259 provider seam to `AbilityContext`; (3) Reconcile DOS-209 landing-order with wave plan. **Not recommended** — the catalogue gap is one-way-door; ungated mutators ship and W3+W4+W5 compose on broken substrate.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:103:2. **Provider seam:** confirm `select_provider` moves to `&AbilityContext` per ADR-0104 / DOS-259 ticket text. Y/N.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:128:- **ADRs cited:** 0104 (ExecutionMode + ServiceContext), 0091 (IntelligenceProvider), 0106 (Prompt Fingerprinting + Provider Interface)
