.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:47:- **Mutation catalogue:** DOS-209's load-bearing invariant is "every mutator gets `check_mutation_allowed()?`." A non-exhaustive catalogue means W2-A ships with **ungated mutators** — the exact failure mode DOS-209 exists to prevent. This is the kind of substrate gap the W3 claims layer + W4 Trust Compiler + W5 pilots will compound on top of.
.docs/plans/wave-W2/escalations/DOS-209-DOS-259-l6-decision.md:49:- **Landing order:** Whichever issue lands first determines the merge-conflict surface on `services/intelligence.rs`. W2-A first means W2-B rebases past 60+ `check_mutation_allowed()?` insertions, some of which are inside functions W2-B is restructuring or deleting. W2-B first means W2-A's sweep is on a smaller surface (PTY orchestration block already gone).
